    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0477" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1039.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-25T15:00:00-04:49">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Before receipt of your November 24, 5 p.m., this morning, Department’s
                    instruction of November 21, 7 p.m., had already been complied with in an
                    interview with the Minister of Foreign Affairs, who expressed gratification at
                    the decision. Particular stress was laid by me as to the character of
                    credentials and it was well understood <pb facs="0478" n="362" xml:id="pg362"/>
                    that they must be satisfactory to the Department before recognition of Theodore
                    as President would be extended. Minister of Foreign Affairs advised President
                    Theodore accordingly and arranged an audience for me this evening. I was
                    informed of the good disposition of President Theodore for the appointment of
                    the commission as desired and was told that he already had in mind the names of
                    persons to serve thereon.</p>
                <p>On receipt of Department’s November 24, 5 p.m., I caused postponement of
                    interview with the President until receipt of further instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
